{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/985926-2e-dreamwalking-and-other-splats","id":985926,"title":"[2e] Dreamwalking and Other Splats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T20:56:44-07:00","id":985926,"title":"[2e] Dreamwalking and Other Splats","content":"So, we have the rules for Changeling 2e's Dreamwalking system, and I'm pretty enamored of it myself. It felt like an irrelevant sideshow in the first edition, but here it's presented up front with all kinds of interesting uses for it. It also gives us a sense of the relation between dreams and the Hedge with Dream Bastions and so on. However, all of this just gives me a bunch of questions that are nagging at me now. How does all of this interact with, say, a Mage who uses the Mind Arcanum to enter into peoples' dreams? A Demon who uses an Exploit to travel to other realms? Or a Beast whose Horror is going around eating people while they sleep, or using Skeleton Key to access strange worlds, or following along with their new buddy's dream journeys?<br /> <br /> Where exactly does that all fit in? Does the Mage have both Dream Health and Physical Health too, or just the one? Does the Beast appear as their Horror with all the appropriate mechanics in the dream? Can they go through the Bastion and into the Hedge from there, or vice versa? Things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T21:07:16-07:00","id":985932,"title":"","content":"Mage would use their dream form mechanics as they are only there in mind not body, while the beast would use the horror rules. Not sure with demons.<br /> <br /> They wouldn't be able to go into the hedge from a bastion directly (though mages could potentially do it in that they can do basically everything given enough thought, though beasts would probably be able to travel to the hedge from a dream through primordial pathways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-12-2016, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T21:47:50-07:00","id":985942,"title":"","content":"A mage couldn't leave a Dream for the Hedge because they aren't in the Dream physically. A physical form is required to go tromping through the Hedge after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:22:29-07:00","id":986115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/985926-2e-dreamwalking-and-other-splats?p=985942#post985942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage couldn't leave a Dream for the Hedge because they aren't in the Dream physically. A physical form is required to go tromping through the Hedge after all</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. The Beast core book also hints thatindepenant horrors some times find a way into the hedge, becoming hedge beasts eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}